 as their  first language so we have to do the work  of going into communities engaging with  those  individuals and ensuring that we have  good access to the vaccines another  reason in london is that many especially  our younger people may have become  infected with the virus during the  course of the pandemic and so they may  feel less inclined to take the vaccine  because they believe they're already  protected  because they've been exposed and for  this group we're ensuring that we have  strong messages about the power of the  vaccination combined with prior  infection to help to protect you moving  forward so these are other reasons why  people aren't getting the vaccines and i  think we need to focus on those and work  with those individuals and communities  rather than trying to convince people  who are absolutely not willing to take  the vaccine  professor fenton thank you so much  thank you
 

